mindmap
  root(("File System"))
    File Concept
      Attributes
        Name / ID / Type
        Location / Size
        Protection / Timestamps
      Operations
        Create / Open
        Read / Write
        Seek / Delete / Close
      Access Methods
        Sequential
          Read next / Write next
          Text editors / media
        Direct
          Read n / Write n
          Databases by record
        Indexed
          Key -> Block index
          DBMS multi-level
    Directory Structure
      Single-Level
        Flat, naming conflicts
      Two-Level
        UFD per user
        MFD index
      Tree-Structured
        Arbitrary depth
        Unix / Windows
      Acyclic-Graph
        Shared subdirs via links
        Hard links vs Symlinks
    Disk Allocation
      Contiguous
        Fast sequential access
        External fragmentation
      Linked
        Each block points to next
        No fragmentation, slow random
      Indexed
        Index block per file
        Supports direct access
    VFS Layer
      ext4 / btrfs / xfs / ntfs
      Uniform system call API
      Mount table
    Protection
      Unix rwx (owner/group/other)
      ACLs (fine-grained)
      Capabilities
